From ccd67438420faabdaeda5f53cf9c8445f9018a53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:47:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03478/11362] [outer-loop] Tier-A result: energy-as-heuristic
 is perception-gated + inconsistent -> lead with #2

Ran experiment_tierA_target_energy_heuristic on vc33 + 6 color/reflect variants.
Finding (mild negative for #1): BFS wins vc33-L1 everywhere (<=95 expansions), so no
generation differentiation; the target-energy heuristic is INCONSISTENT even where the
featurizer works (3x efficiency win on base, but 14x LOSS on color_v2 -- the permuted
colors mislead it); and the hard games have no featurizer to test at all. So
energy-as-directed-heuristic (#1) is perception-gated and not a reliable generation
unlock. Decision: lead with #2 (energy-as-fitness QD, perception-independent).

verdict: complete: target_energy_heuristic_helps_on_featurizer_ok_only_no_variant_transfer_perception_gated

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
